# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values.
# This file holds no secrets, because everything Vite puts in the browser bundle
# is public by definition — anyone can read it in devtools.
#
# Locally the backend runs on port 5000, so this is the default and you can skip
# the file entirely while developing.
# Optional. Leave it unset and the app calls its own origin (see below).
#
# Both folders deploy as ONE Vercel project, so the browser talks to /api/* on the
# same domain it loaded the page from and the backend's URL never has to be known.
# Locally `vite dev` proxies /api to localhost:5000, so this stays unset there too.
#
# VITE_API_URL only needs a value if you want the frontend to call a *different*
# backend (for instance a standalone one deployed as its own project):
# VITE_API_URL=https://<backend-project>.vercel.app

